            <ArticleTitle>Unusual mechanism of isolated torsion of fallopian tube following minor trauma. Herniation through a broad ligament tear.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>637-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Isolated torsion of the fallopian tube without ovarian involvement and associated pathology is a rare event. We report an 18-year-old single female who presented with acute lower abdominal pain during menstruation after a minor trauma of the pelvis. It was diagnosed as isolated torsion of normal right tube during laparatomy due to herniation of the tube through a tear in the broad ligament.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
